  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 118 PM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nAs we head into the end of the weekend and into the beginning of\nnext week, northwesterly flow will continue over the region as\nan upper level ridge begins to build over the Plains. This will\nkeep the dry conditions, with temperatures warming each day as\nmidlevel heights rise. With only a 3-degree difference between \nthe NBM MaxT interquartile spread, there's high confidence in \nafternoon highs climbing back into the 70s by Monday and \nTuesday, which is 5-10 degrees above the climatological normal \nfor this time of year. \n\nMore uncertainty exists midweek towards the end of next week, as\nan upper level shortwave trough slides across the southern\nCONUS while additional upper level energy pushes in from the\nnorth. There are discrepancies between ensembles regarding the \ntrack of these systems, which will influence precipitation \nchances (currently <15%) and temperatures. The NBM \ninterquartile spread shows a 10-20 degree difference during this\ntimeframe, leading to fairly low confidence in afternoon highs.",
